# Findings accepted by the publish-images Trivy gate (.github/workflows/publish-images.yml).
#
# Every entry needs a reason it does not apply, the version that fixes it, and an
# expiry date. Trivy stops ignoring an entry after its `exp:` date, so the gate
# fails again and the decision has to be revisited rather than forgotten.

# Spring Framework spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (Spring Boot 3.5.16). Fixed only in
# Spring Framework 7.0.9, i.e. a Spring Boot 4 migration. Not reachable here:
# the services are JSON REST APIs with no view rendering at all - no XsltView,
# no view resolvers or template engines, no Server-Sent Events.
#
# CVE-2026-47884: RCE/SSRF via XsltView with a "/**" mapping that renders views.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
# CVE-2026-47890: SSE stream corruption with view fragments.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
